{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed the WI-878 intent spine set. No statuses or IDs changed. Arms map: [terra878-arms.md](/C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-24b-leg18/terra878-arms.md).\n\nChanged cells (quoted spans show before → after):\n\n- LLR-069 `code_symbol`: `\".../_tree_text/_tree_tomls/_ruled_texts/_correspondence_problem/...\"` → `\".../_tree_text/_correspondence_problem/...\"`. Removes the two helpers P5 deletes.\n- LLR-069 `detail`: `\"the findings file beside that verdict records the ruled finding with that F#'s text\"` → `\"the findings file the verdict's binding records, read in the same reading as the verdict and its binding, records the ruled finding with that F#'s text\"`; added refusal/no-other-file clauses. Aligns the gate contract with the binding-record authority.\n- LLR-310 `code_symbol`: `\"read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX\"` → `\"read_requested/read_findings_file/REQUESTED_SUFFIX\"`. Names the planned binding reader.\n- LLR-310 `detail`: added `\"A dispute binding also records the findings file its composed brief names… A brief that names none binds none, which every reader reads as absent.\"` Defines record creation, preservation, and absence.\n- LLR-314 `code_symbol`: `\"request_line/requested_ids/parse\"` → `\"request_line/file_line/requested_ids/requested_file/parse\"`. Names the planned grammar functions.\n- LLR-314 `detail`: added `\"The composed brief's findings-file line names the reference it carries; its first such line supplies the path, and no or empty line supplies none.\"` Defines the line grammar without naming an implementation carrier.\n- LLR-315 `detail`: added `\"The request value carries, after the requested ids, the findings-file line naming the one reference the assembler read.\"` Defines ordering and provenance of the brief record.\n- TC-069 `method`: added the two-round, cross-round, absent-record, four bad-record, HEAD pass-record, and entry-point cases.\n- TC-069 `expected`: added the corresponding pass/refusal outcomes.\n- TC-069 `evidence`: appended T1–T5 and T8:\n  `test_two_dispute_rounds_reusing_ids_each_resolve_their_own_finding`,\n  `test_round_ones_verdict_cited_for_round_twos_same_id_finding_refuses`,\n  `test_a_binding_without_the_findings_record_refuses_and_reads_no_sibling`,\n  `test_a_recorded_findings_file_that_cannot_show_the_finding_refuses`,\n  `test_at_the_cap_a_dismissal_bound_without_its_findings_file_is_refused`,\n  `test_the_entry_points_dispute_binding_resolves_only_its_own_rounds_finding`.\n- TC-327 `method` / `expected`: added binding-at-reservation, accepted/failed preservation, and absent-line behavior.\n- TC-327 `evidence`: appended T7, `tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_dispute_binding_records_its_findings_file_through_the_outcome`.\n- TC-334 `method` / `expected`: added composed findings-file line and grammar round-trip behavior.\n- TC-334 `evidence`: appended T6, `tests/test_dispute.py::test_the_dispute_brief_names_the_findings_file_it_was_composed_over`.\n- IF-287 `data`: appended `\"the dispute findings-file record cell and its reader\"`.\n- IF-287 `notes`: appended `\"A findings-file record is carried the same way … an absent record reads as none.\"`\n- IF-290 `data`: added `file_line(path)` and `requested_file(brief_text)`.\n- Flow 6 bind step: `\"bind the judging brief and its judged rows' identities (LLR-306, LLR-359)\"` → `\"bind the judging brief, its judged rows' identities and a dispute brief's findings file (LLR-306, LLR-359, LLR-310)\"`.\n\nSR walk — unchanged as the plan expects:\n\n- SR-232 requirement: combined sitting preservation remains true.\n- SR-232 acceptance: exact declared kinds remains true.\n- SR-232 acceptance: one valid scoped section per kind remains true.\n- SR-232 acceptance: invalid/missing/extra/duplicate sections still refuse.\n- SR-234 requirement: contest/repeat trigger remains true.\n- SR-234 requirement: findings, positions, and change scope remain preserved.\n- SR-234 requirement: exactly-once declared rulings remain true.\n- SR-234 requirement: successor restriction remains true.\n- SR-234 acceptance: complete findings/range/scope composition remains true.\n- SR-234 acceptance: malformed input still refuses without a partial sitting.\n- SR-234 acceptance: verdict completeness and declared-ruling validation remain true.\n- SR-234 acceptance: dispute verdicts still authorize no approval act; successor rules remain true.\n\nChecks run:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict` — exit 0: `clean (971 work item(s), 860 done (89%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).`\n- `trace.py --strict` — exit 0: `Traceability: SN=31 SR=138 LLR=326 TC=353 orphans=0 integrity=0 ... interface-findings=0 ...`\n- `git diff --check` — clean.\n- Pytest was not run, as directed for this intent turn.\n\nThe strict checks retain their pre-build advisory warnings, including the expected LLR-069 carrier mismatch because the old helpers still exist until the builder’s P5 implementation. No unresolved authoring issue remains."}}
